{
  "about": [
    "One adversarial table for attribute text (a plain_text field whose value renders into one attribute of an element) in a managed site, run by",
    "site-starter packages/managed-site-contract (src/attribute-text.ts and fields.ts, the rules Site Guard and a site build hold a declaration and a value to)",
    "and by megaseo-web's CMS (the SQL writer's judge and its TypeScript twin cms_text_rules.ts).",
    "Keep this file byte-identical wherever it is run; change every copy together.",
    "attributeNames: whether a declared constraints.attribute is one a field may write. Exact, case-sensitive; anything else is refused (contract) or makes the field's limits unknown and unsavable (CMS).",
    "valueCases: an attribute text value under limits minLength 1, maxLength 512, newlines forbid unless the case states limits.",
    "expected.reason is the CMS's refusal reason, in cmsTextRefusal's order: line_break; then unsafe_character; then blank; then too_long; then too_short. null is admitted. The contract package is held to outcome only.",
    "policyCases: contract-only; a plain_text field declaring an attribute, and whether the declaration parses."
  ],
  "defaultLimits": {
    "minLength": 1,
    "maxLength": 512,
    "newlines": "forbid"
  },
